brought her to the window now where's that van from first he said we have to collect

00:22:00.190 --> 00:22:07.240
didn't she she wants the old sweet out the way doesn't she i wonder if he's in next door

00:22:07.240 --> 00:22:16.550
the divorce person oh he looks so sad he needs the skills of someone sympathetic

00:22:16.550 --> 00:22:23.240
to cheer him out why don't you start mauling him again i wrote i wouldn't call it mauling

00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:29.830
him just sympathy i get three years for sympathy like that

00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:33.400
Oh, look at that!

00:22:33.400 --> 00:22:36.290
I've got to run it to your person, she's certainly organised.

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:42.180
Liz, what's that awful old truck doing outside Hyacinths?

00:22:42.180 --> 00:22:44.180
Get rid of them!

00:22:44.180 --> 00:22:48.160
They've come for the suite, you offered them our own suite!

00:22:48.160 --> 00:22:49.160
Get rid of them!

00:22:49.160 --> 00:22:50.160
Ye gods!

00:22:50.160 --> 00:22:54.170
With Mrs Barker Finch watching, this is all I need.

00:22:54.170 --> 00:22:57.170
Onslow in some borrowed deathtrap of a vehicle.

00:22:57.170 --> 00:22:58.170
Get rid of them!

00:22:58.170 --> 00:23:00.000
What about us?

00:23:00.580 --> 00:23:02.160
Oh, tell them to come back later,

00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:02.960
after dark.

00:23:04.460 --> 00:23:05.640
Providing there isn't a moon.

00:23:06.620 --> 00:23:08.020
Well, I can't just ask them

00:23:08.020 --> 00:23:10.100
to go away. Richard, you know

00:23:10.100 --> 00:23:12.140
I love my family, but that's no reason

00:23:12.140 --> 00:23:14.160
why I should have to acknowledge them in broad daylight.

00:23:15.220 --> 00:23:16.140
Now, go

00:23:16.140 --> 00:23:18.040
out there and convince

00:23:18.040 --> 00:23:19.320
Mrs Barker Finch

00:23:19.320 --> 00:23:21.470
that they're just people who have

00:23:21.470 --> 00:23:23.370
stopped to ask the way. How am I

00:23:23.370 --> 00:23:25.430
supposed to do that? She's standing by

00:23:25.430 --> 00:23:27.550
her window. She cannot hear what's

00:23:27.550 --> 00:23:30.000
being said. We've got to

00:23:30.030 --> 00:23:34.190
Make it look as though we're just giving directions to passing strangers.

00:23:35.410 --> 00:23:39.220
Oh, watch me dear, I'll show you what I mean.

00:23:39.220 --> 00:23:47.340
You people.

00:23:49.380 --> 00:23:51.520
You people.

00:23:51.520 --> 00:23:54.060
The man's gone.

00:23:54.060 --> 00:23:56.520
Would've gone.

00:23:56.520 --> 00:23:58.610
She has no romance in her life.

00:23:58.610 --> 00:23:59.890
Mine would've gone.

00:24:02.520 --> 00:24:05.040
She's not the only one with no romance in her life.

00:24:06.440 --> 00:24:07.340
What about last week?

00:24:11.080 --> 00:24:14.870
Oh, keeping records now, aren't we?

00:24:15.380 --> 00:24:16.570
The blonde one's there.

00:24:16.930 --> 00:24:18.450
The one that's always trying to seduce me.

00:24:20.110 --> 00:24:20.510
No.

00:24:21.930 --> 00:24:25.630
If they're family, why is Harrison acting as if they're strangers?

00:24:26.480 --> 00:24:28.760
That's the impression she likes to give.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:35.570
You don't think the blonde one will try and force her way in, do you?

00:24:35.570 --> 00:24:39.050
I hardly think so.

00:24:39.050 --> 00:24:41.050
I wish you'd sound a bit more optimistic.

00:24:41.050 --> 00:24:44.770
The point is, my suite hasn't arrived yet.

00:24:44.770 --> 00:24:46.870
I'm expecting the van any minute.

00:24:46.870 --> 00:24:56.150
So if you could clear this area and perhaps pop back later, after dark, well, after dark,

00:24:56.150 --> 00:25:00.000
have your suite waiting.

00:25:00.220 --> 00:25:07.050
collect it then and take it off down there. Take the first turn left and proceed along

00:25:07.050 --> 00:25:12.630
until you come as far as. And instead of standing there looking at me with your mouths wide

00:25:12.630 --> 00:25:17.510
open, why don't you all get back into that vehicle, drive off in that direction, take

00:25:17.510 --> 00:25:20.650
the first turning left, which will bring you to you know where.

00:25:33.320 --> 00:25:33.960
It has.

00:25:34.620 --> 00:25:35.680
Her mind's gone.

00:25:36.480 --> 00:25:37.560
I think it's sad.

00:25:38.470 --> 00:25:39.810
Yes, but we still get the sweet.

00:25:41.380 --> 00:25:44.450
I'll give my regards to him that's divorced from now.

00:25:48.780 --> 00:25:53.780
Goodness, that's over.

00:25:54.860 --> 00:25:58.960
Fancy bringing a vehicle in that condition into a residential area.

00:26:00.120 --> 00:26:02.700
If Sheridan were here, he'd be appalled.

00:26:02.700 --> 00:26:09.740
Richard, I want you to stay here and look like someone expecting a van.

00:26:09.740 --> 00:26:10.740
Hyacinth.

00:26:10.740 --> 00:26:13.760
What should keep Mrs Barker Finch at her window?

00:26:13.760 --> 00:26:30.000
Send round another portion of stir-fried squid with fish balls and broccoli.

00:26:30.640 --> 00:26:32.980
This is not the Green Lotus Chinese takeaway.

00:26:34.780 --> 00:26:38.340
I may only be one digit removed, but believe me, it's a whole other world.

00:26:39.660 --> 00:26:41.950
I heard that and it wasn't Chinese.

00:26:42.850 --> 00:26:44.630
Your suite is here.

00:26:44.850 --> 00:26:46.970
Oh, at last.

00:26:47.440 --> 00:26:50.290
Let's hope that Mrs Barker Finch is still at the window.

00:26:50.570 --> 00:26:53.370
Yeah, just the suite's here, not the van.

00:26:53.510 --> 00:26:54.050
Not the van?

00:26:54.170 --> 00:26:54.370
No.

00:26:55.050 --> 00:26:57.400
Not the van with the royal warrant?

00:26:57.400 --> 00:27:00.000
No, I'm afraid not. It's had an accident in the next June.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:05.010
Oh, no. But surely their relief van displays the Royal Wallet.

00:27:05.010 --> 00:27:10.010
Well, it's not actually their relief van, it's just somebody who's come to the rescue.

00:27:10.010 --> 00:27:24.500
Oh, we love them, dear, and when the suite's in place, we'll have to ask them in and they can have tea out of my Royal Doolton with the hand-painted periwinkles.

00:27:24.500 --> 00:27:30.000
Oh, after all my trouble, Mrs. Barker,

00:27:30.190 --> 00:27:39.810
at the window and not a royal warrant in sight. Never mind, it's here.

00:27:39.810 --> 00:27:49.840
You should have seen that! Hey, good job, we were passing.

00:27:49.840 --> 00:27:59.700
Yes, isn't it? Well, isn't it? I suppose so. I suppose Hanslow meant well.

00:28:00.730 --> 00:28:02.550
You'd better tip the furniture man, Richard.

00:28:03.010 --> 00:28:03.530
Again?

00:28:05.840 --> 00:28:08.040
Does Onslow still get tea when he's finished?

00:28:09.440 --> 00:28:12.960
Of course he can have tea afterwards.

00:28:14.490 --> 00:28:16.890
But not out of my royal doelton.

00:28:17.730 --> 00:28:22.560
And he won't sit on my new suite either.
